n-trans.kicad_sch and the erc.json excerpt, classifying errors versus library/grid hygiene warnings.\",\"Reviewed DRC results (142 violations, 13 errors, 114 parity issues) including error-type counts (padstack, annular_width, starved_thermal) and the schematic-parity entries in the drc.json excerpt.\",\"Cross-checked exported connectivity (work/netlist/connectivity.json, 139 components / 199 nets) for the dual-wideband CAN2 bus: transceiver pin nets, VCC(+5V)/VIO(+3.3V) rails, NUP2105L protector nets, 47 pF filter caps, and DNP status of termination resistors R36/R37.\",\"Checked saved-board placement of CAN2 components (U20/U21 transceiver positions, R36/R37 terminator pad nets and positions, C29/C30/C33/C34 filter caps) in the geometry.json excerpt.\",\"Verified wideband module strapping (U1 SEL pin to GND, U2 SEL pin to +5V) and heater/LSU net fan-out between J1 and U1/U2 in connectivity.json.\",\"Cross-checked README feature claims (dual CAN, internal CAN2 widebands, lowside adder, IGBT outputs, stepper) against netlist nets and components.\",\"Reviewed the disposable VR Conditioner.kicad_sch sheet-path alias usage in the 10-instance hierarchy (netlist schematic_files, design.xml sheet sources).\"],\"limitations\":[\"Several artifacts were truncated in the packet: drc.json (100000/142607 bytes, the 13 error-severity entries for padstack/annular_width/starved_thermal are not visible), erc.json (100000/226344), geometry.json (100000/1657568, tracks/vias/zones not included), design.xml (84913/252017); geometry execution.json and console.log were omitted entirely. Error locations for the DRC errors are therefore known only by count and type.\",\"No trace width, copper ampacity, thermal, or return-path evaluation was possible: the geometry excerpt contains only footprint/pad data, no track or zone geometry, and no current requirements were declared. Per instructions, no ampacity or thermal qualification is inferred.\",\"Zone fill was evaluated as saved; the read-only candidate forbids a refill, so the 3 starved_thermal errors reflect the saved fill state and could change after a refill.\",\"The verification environment lacks the project libraries Simon, hellen-one-common, fome_modules and header_placement, so ~200 lib_symbol/lib_footprint mismatch or issue warnings could not be resolved against library sources; cached symbols/footprints were accepted as-is.\",\"External harness behavior (CAN bus length, external termination, ignition transients, EMC) is out of scope per the declared limitations and was not assessed.\",\"The Polygonus brain module (J2) internals are not part of this donor packet, so protection/termination possibly located on the module (e.g., for CAN1) could not be verified.\"],\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"PHY-001\",\"title\":\"Saved board has 13 DRC error-severity violations: padstack, annular width, and starved thermal\",\"location\":\"Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb (specific items truncated out of supplied drc.json excerpt)\",\"condition\":\"DRC with --severity-all reports 13 error-severity violations on the saved board: padstack x5, annular_width x5, starved_thermal x3 (by_type/by_severity in the drc check record; console confirms 142 total violations).\",\"mechanism\":\"Annular ring below minimum risks drill breakout and open or intermittent plated-through connections after fabrication; padstack errors risk fab rejection or unreliable via construction; starved thermal reliefs mean pads join their copper zones through insufficient spokes, constricting the electrical connection and degrading solderability on what are typically ground/power pads.\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"assessment\":\"defect\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/drc/drc.json\",\"locator\":\"by_type: padstack=5, annular_width=5, starved_thermal=3; by_severity: error=13 (summarized in drc check details; individual entries beyond byte 100000 of the excerpt)\"},{\"path\":\"work/drc/console.log\",\"locator\":\"line 1: 'Found 142 violations'\"}],\"reasoning\":\"These are native tool errors on the saved copper, not tool failures. The exact coordinates are not in the supplied excerpt, so the count and classification come from the tool's own summary; the physical failure modes they encode (drill breakout, starved zone connection) are manufacturing and connectivity risks independent of location. Zone-fill-as-saved is a caveat for the starved_thermal subset only.\"},{\"id\":\"PHY-002\",\"title\":\"Internal dual-wideband CAN2 bus has both 120 ohm terminators (R36, R37) unpopulated\",\"location\":\"wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch (R36 at 115.57,86.36, two sheet instances R36/R37); board: R36 at (175.01,140.67), R37 at (81.62,140.55)\",\"condition\":\"The README states the two wideband controllers are connected internally to CAN bus #2. The CAN2+/CAN2- nets join U20.7/6, U21.7/6, J2.73/74, J1.15/11, protectors D10/D11 and filter caps, plus terminators R36.1/2 and R37.1/2. Both R36 and R37 are marked (dnp yes)(in_bom no) in the native sheet and dnp:true in the netlist, so the saved board ships with zero on-board CAN2 termination.\",\"mechanism\":\"U20 and U21 sit at roughly opposite board edges (R36 near x=175 mm, R37/U21 near x=75-82 mm), so the populated pair would form correct split end-termination. With both DNP, the internal multi-node bus between the two wideband MCUs, the ECU module, and the harness pins is unterminated unless the external harness supplies both 120 ohm ends; reflections on an unterminated or singly-terminated bus can corrupt wideband CAN traffic at typical 500 kbit rates.\",\"severity\":\"major\",\"assessment\":\"concern\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch\",\"locator\":\"symbol R36 (uuid d69380f9-5487-4782-9ce9-0690df62e543): value 120, (in_bom no)(dnp yes), instances R36/R37\"},{\"path\":\"work/netlist/connectivity.json\",\"locator\":\"nets /CAN2+ and /CAN2- include R36.1/R37.1 and R36.2/R37.2; components R36, R37 dnp:true\"},{\"path\":\"work/geometry/geometry.json\",\"locator\":\"R36 dnp:true pads on /CAN2+ and /CAN2- at (175.01,142.13); U21 at (75.48,140.27); C33/C34 near x=81-82\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/project/README.md\",\"locator\":\"'Dual wideband O2 sensor controllers ... connected internally to CAN bus #2'\"}],\"reasoning\":\"Marked as a concern rather than a defect because the DNP may be a deliberate builder option (CAN2 is also exposed on J1 pins 11/15 for external nodes, where double internal termination would conflict with harness terminators). However, no documentation in the packet instructs the builder to terminate externally, and the advertised internal wideband function depends on a properly terminated bus, so the as-saved population is a real signal-integrity risk that the scope explicitly asks to be reviewed.\"},{\"id\":\"PHY-003\",\"title\":\"Five ERC error-severity violations: undriven power inputs, power-output conflict, unconnected fault pin\",\"location\":\"Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_sch root sheet\",\"condition\":\"ERC reports 5 errors: GND power input #PWR01 not driven (36.83,78.74); A1 pin 8 VMOT power input not driven (48.26,219.71); J2 pin 90 12V_IGN power input not driven (293.37,173.99); J2 pins 40/41 both Power-output type tied together on 5V_SENSOR_1 (262.89,128.27/130.81); A1 pin 2 ~FLT output unconnected with no no-connect marker (38.1,224.79).\",\"mechanism\":\"The undriven power-input errors indicate battery/harness-fed nets (12V_KEY, VMOT via 12V_MR_FUSE) and GND lack PWR_FLAG markers, so the tool cannot confirm a power source; the pin_to_pin error is two power-output pins of the same module symbol paralleled; the unconnected DRV8825 ~FLT pin means stepper-driver fault reporting is physically unmonitored and the omission is unmarked, so it cannot be distinguished from an accidental open.\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"assessment\":\"defect\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/erc/erc.json\",\"locator\":\"root sheet '/': power_pin_not_driven x3 (uuids ad746bdd, acdd6b6d, 3d2dd476), pin_to_pin (2f453565/b5fc1cf2), pin_not_connected A1 pin 2 (a25f94e0)\"},{\"path\":\"work/erc/console.log\",\"locator\":\"'Found 353 violations'\"}],\"reasoning\":\"These are confirmed native errors. Electrically, the undriven-power and paralleled-output cases are explainable (harness-fed rails, duplicated module pins) and therefore minor, but they remain unresolved errors that mask any future genuine power-sourcing fault; the unmarked ~FLT open is a small functional gap (no stepper fault detection) rather than a hazard.\"},{\"id\":\"PHY-004\",\"title\":\"Main module footprint on board differs from schematic assignment (J2)\",\"location\":\"Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb, footprint J2 at (136.57,99.21)\",\"condition\":\"Schematic parity reports: 'Simon:Polygonus-With-USB-SWD doesn't match footprint given by symbol (fome_modules:polygonus)' plus an exclude-from-BOM attribute mismatch for footprint J2.\",\"mechanism\":\"The board carries a different footprint variant for the central ECU brain-module connector than the schematic assigns. Net-level parity passed (0 unconnected items), so pad-to-net mapping currently agrees, but the divergent footprint identity means mechanical outline, extra pads (USB/SWD variant), or future re-sync from schematic could silently alter the board, and the Simon library is absent from the verification environment so the placed footprint could not be validated against any source.\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"assessment\":\"concern\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/drc/drc.json\",\"locator\":\"schematic_parity entries for 'Footprint J2' (uuid f447e585-df78-4239-b8cb-4653b3837bb1), types footprint_symbol_mismatch\"},{\"path\":\"work/drc/execution.json\",\"locator\":\"argv includes --schematic-parity; exit_code 0\"}],\"reasoning\":\"Concern rather than defect: connectivity parity holds and the substitution is plausibly an intentional variant with USB/SWD breakout, but the schematic/board divergence on the single most connected component (107 pins) is a configuration-management risk, especially with the source library unavailable for comparison.\"},{\"id\":\"PHY-005\",\"title\":\"Library environment gaps leave ~200 symbol/footprint integrity checks unresolved\",\"location\":\"ERC/DRC runs (sandboxed environment, project libraries absent)\",\"condition\":\"ERC: lib_symbol_mismatch x89, lib_symbol_issues x14, footprint_link_issues x8 ('configuration does not include the footprint library Simon' / symbol library hellen-one-common, Connector, Device:CP etc.). DRC: lib_footprint_mismatch x106, lib_footprint_issues x9.\",\"mechanism\":\"With the Simon, hellen-one-common, fome_modules and related libraries missing from the verification sandbox, every cached symbol and footprint from those libraries is unverifiable against its source, and stock-library parts additionally mismatch their current library copies (KiCad 10 vs design-era KiCad 9 libraries). A stale or edited cached footprint (e.g., the 112-pin Molex J1 or the wideband module footprints) would pass this review undetected as long as internal pad/net mapping is self-consistent.\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"assessment\":\"concern\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/erc/erc.json\",\"locator\":\"by_type lib_symbol_mismatch=89, lib_symbol_issues=14, footprint_link_issues=8; e.g. 'The current configuration does not include the footprint library Simon' for J1 (uuid 6971898b)\"},{\"path\":\"work/drc/drc.json\",\"locator\":\"by_type lib_footprint_mismatch=106, lib_footprint_issues=9; e.g. 'The current configuration does not include the footprint library Simon' for J1 (uuid 93ba26da)\"}],\"reasoning\":\"This is a verification-coverage challenge rather than a board fault: the checks ran, but a large class of library-integrity assertions is vacuous in this environment, so the 'native rule coverage' claim in the scope is weaker than the raw run counts suggest.\"},{\"id\":\"PHY-006\",\"title\":\"229 off-grid wire/pin endpoints in the schematic\",\"location\":\"Multiple sheets, concentrated in root and VR Conditioner areas (e.g. wires at 286.385,107.315; 107.315,80.01; 165.735,75.565)\",\"condition\":\"ERC reports 229 endpoint_off_grid warnings: wire ends and symbol pins (including R25/R26/R31/R34 pins, JP1, PWR symbols, C24/C25 pins) sit off the connection grid.\",\"mechanism\":\"Off-grid endpoints currently resolve to connected nets (netlist is complete, 0 unconnected board items), but they are fragile: any future edit or symbol move can silently break a junction that visually appears connected, and several off-grid points sit on the VR conditioner analog front end where a silent open would disable crank-signal processing.\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"assessment\":\"concern\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/erc/erc.json\",\"locator\":\"by_type endpoint_off_grid=229; e.g. uuids 15d9afbe (286.385,107.315), 34654827 (R25 pin 1 at 107.315,80.01), c2f74bd3 (R34 pin 1 at 165.735,75.565)\"},{\"path\":\"work/netlist/connectivity.json\",\"locator\":\"all affected nets (Net-(R25-Pad1), Net-(U10-IN-) etc.) presently resolve with expected members\"}],\"reasoning\":\"No present-day connectivity fault is evidenced (DRC shows 0 unconnected items), so this is a latent-risk concern about schematic hygiene, not a defect in the saved netlist.\"},{\"id\":\"PHY-007\",\"title\":\"Hierarchy depends on disposable 'VR Conditioner.kicad_sch' byte-copy alias of the lowercase original\",\"location\":\"project/VR Conditioner.kicad_sch (alias of VR conditioner.kicad_sch)\",\"condition\":\"The candidate adds VR Conditioner.kicad_sch as a byte copy of the existing lowercase file so the 10-instance hierarchy resolves; ERC/netlist runs list project/VR Conditioner.kicad_sch and design.xml records sheet 4 source 'VR Conditioner.kicad_sch'. The declared limitations confirm the original checkout's filename discrepancy remains open.\",\"mechanism\":\"Two byte-identical files with case-differing names coexist in the project. On case-insensitive filesystems they collide; on case-sensitive systems future edits can land in whichever copy a given tool resolves, silently forking the VR conditioner sheet (MAX9924 crank input chain, C23-C25, R25-R34, JP1). All connectivity verified here is against the alias, not the original file path.\",\"severity\":\"minor\",\"assessment\":\"concern\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/netlist/design.xml\",\"locator\":\"sheet number 4 '/VR Conditioner/' source 'VR Conditioner.kicad_sch'\"},{\"path\":\"work/netlist/connectivity.json\",\"locator\":\"components C23-C25, R25-R34, U10, JP1 on sheet /VR Conditioner/ (uuid 76f66c7e-94ea-4f9a-aa2e-a01725934e38)\"}],\"reasoning\":\"The alias is explicitly declared as a disposable workaround, so this is not a new defect, but the physical design content of the VR conditioner now has two potential sources of truth; the verified netlist applies only to the alias as supplied.\"},{\"id\":\"PHY-008\",\"title\":\"Main CAN bus (CAN1) has no board-level ESD protection or filtering, unlike CAN2\",\"location\":\"Root sheet nets /CAN+ and /CAN-\",\"condition\":\"Nets /CAN+ (J1.47, J2.93) and /CAN- (J1.46, J2.94) run directly from the harness connector to the brain-module connector with no TVS, filter capacitors, or termination footprints on the base board, whereas CAN2 carries NUP2105L protectors (D10/D11), 47 pF filters, and terminator footprints.\",\"mechanism\":\"If the Polygonus module does not include transceiver-side protection, the primary vehicle CAN lines enter the module unprotected against harness ESD/transients; the asymmetry versus CAN2 suggests protection was assumed to live on the module, which cannot be confirmed from this packet.\",\"severity\":\"info\",\"assessment\":\"concern\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/netlist/connectivity.json\",\"locator\":\"'/CAN+': [J1.47, J2.93]; '/CAN-': [J1.46, J2.94]; contrast '/CAN2+'/'/CAN2-' with D10/D11, C29/C30/C33/C34, R36/R37\"}],\"reasoning\":\"No requirement for base-board CAN1 protection is declared, and the module (out of scope) plausibly provides it, so this is recorded only as an informational observation about the asymmetric protection scheme and the coverage boundary, not as a fault.\"}]}","structured_output":{"schema":"agent-ee.review/1","candidate_id":"2767e5a30de2c3bcdee814eda2dbc63cc460f744b8029c74079b8feea3e0ae9b","run_id":"127a9e8e-5b06-4239-87ce-8ad95a4c01af","packet_sha256":"45933e29c78fa681b6a813c861b829f25710437d532eee33a5be27ae534e3bec","role":"physical","coverage":["Reviewed ERC results (353 violations, 5 errors) against the supplied native sheet wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch and the erc.json excerpt, classifying errors versus library/grid hygiene warnings.","Reviewed DRC results (142 violations, 13 errors, 114 parity issues) including error-type counts (padstack, annular_width, starved_thermal) and the schematic-parity entries in the drc.json excerpt.","Cross-checked exported connectivity (work/netlist/connectivity.json, 139 components / 199 nets) for the dual-wideband CAN2 bus: transceiver pin nets, VCC(+5V)/VIO(+3.3V) rails, NUP2105L protector nets, 47 pF filter caps, and DNP status of termination resistors R36/R37.","Checked saved-board placement of CAN2 components (U20/U21 transceiver positions, R36/R37 terminator pad nets and positions, C29/C30/C33/C34 filter caps) in the geometry.json excerpt.","Verified wideband module strapping (U1 SEL pin to GND, U2 SEL pin to +5V) and heater/LSU net fan-out between J1 and U1/U2 in connectivity.json.","Cross-checked README feature claims (dual CAN, internal CAN2 widebands, lowside adder, IGBT outputs, stepper) against netlist nets and components.","Reviewed the disposable VR Conditioner.kicad_sch sheet-path alias usage in the 10-instance hierarchy (netlist schematic_files, design.xml sheet sources)."],"limitations":["Several artifacts were truncated in the packet: drc.json (100000/142607 bytes, the 13 error-severity entries for padstack/annular_width/starved_thermal are not visible), erc.json (100000/226344), geometry.json (100000/1657568, tracks/via