severity":"major","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch","locator":"symbol R36 (uuid d69380f9-5487-4782-9ce9-0690df62e543): value 120, (in_bom no)(dnp yes), instances R36/R37"},{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"nets /CAN2+ and /CAN2- include R36.1/R37.1 and R36.2/R37.2; components R36, R37 dnp:true"},{"path":"work/geometry/geometry.json","locator":"R36 dnp:true pads on /CAN2+ and /CAN2- at (175.01,142.13); U21 at (75.48,140.27); C33/C34 near x=81-82"},{"path":"inputs/project/README.md","locator":"'Dual wideband O2 sensor controllers ... connected internally to CAN bus #2'"}],"reasoning":"Marked as a concern rather than a defect because the DNP may be a deliberate builder option (CAN2 is also exposed on J1 pins 11/15 for external nodes, where double internal termination would conflict with harness terminators). However, no documentation in the packet instructs the builder to terminate externally, and the advertised internal wideband function depends on a properly terminated bus, so the as-saved population is a real signal-integrity risk that the scope explicitly asks to be reviewed."},{"id":"PHY-003","title":"Five ERC error-severity violations: undriven power inputs, power-output conflict, unconnected fault pin","location":"Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_sch root sheet","condition":"ERC reports 5 errors: GND power input #PWR01 not driven (36.83,78.74); A1 pin 8 VMOT power input not driven (48.26,219.71); J2 pin 90 12V_IGN power input not driven (293.37,173.99); J2 pins 40/41 both Power-output type tied together on 5V_SENSOR_1 (262.89,128.27/130.81); A1 pin 2 ~FLT output unconnected with no no-connect marker (38.1,224.79).","mechanism":"The undriven power-input errors indicate battery/harness-fed nets (12V_KEY, VMOT via 12V_MR_FUSE) and GND lack PWR_FLAG markers, so the tool cannot confirm a power source; the pin_to_pin error is two power-output pins of the same module symbol paralleled; the unconnected DRV8825 ~FLT pin means stepper-driver fault reporting is physically unmonitored and the omission is unmarked, so it cannot be distinguished from an accidental open.","severity":"minor","assessment":"defect","evidence":[{"path":"work/erc/erc.json","locator":"root sheet '/': power_pin_not_driven x3 (uuids ad746bdd, acdd6b6d, 3d2dd476), pin_to_pin (2f453565/b5fc1cf2), pin_not_connected A1 pin 2 (a25f94e0)"},{"path":"work/erc/console.log","locator":"'Found 353 violations'"}],"reasoning":"These are confirmed native errors. Electrically, the undriven-power and paralleled-output cases are explainable (harness-fed rails, duplicated module pins) and therefore minor, but they remain unresolved errors that mask any future genuine power-sourcing fault; the unmarked ~FLT open is a small functional gap (no stepper fault detection) rather than a hazard."},{"id":"PHY-004","title":"Main module footprint on board differs from schematic assignment (J2)","location":"Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb, footprint J2 at (136.57,99.21)","condition":"Schematic parity reports: 'Simon:Polygonus-With-USB-SWD doesn't match footprint given by symbol (fome_modules:polygonus)' plus an exclude-from-BOM attribute mismatch for footprint J2.","mechanism":"The board carries a different footprint variant for the central ECU brain-module connector than the schematic assigns. Net-level parity passed (0 unconnected items), so pad-to-net mapping currently agrees, but the divergent footprint identity means mechanical outline, extra pads (USB/SWD variant), or future re-sync from schematic could silently alter the board, and the Simon library is absent from the verification environment so the placed footprint could not be validated against any source.","severity":"minor","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"work/drc/drc.json","locator":"schematic_parity entries for 'Footprint J2' (uuid f447e585-df78-4239-b8cb-4653b3837bb1), types footprint_symbol_mismatch"},{"path":"work/drc/execution.json","locator":"arg