this environment, so the 'native rule coverage' claim in the scope is weaker than the raw run counts suggest."},{"id":"PHY-006","title":"229 off-grid wire/pin endpoints in the schematic","location":"Multiple sheets, concentrated in root and VR Conditioner areas (e.g. wires at 286.385,107.315; 107.315,80.01; 165.735,75.565)","condition":"ERC reports 229 endpoint_off_grid warnings: wire ends and symbol pins (including R25/R26/R31/R34 pins, JP1, PWR symbols, C24/C25 pins) sit off the connection grid.","mechanism":"Off-grid endpoints currently resolve to connected nets (netlist is complete, 0 unconnected board items), but they are fragile: any future edit or symbol move can silently break a junction that visually appears connected, and several off-grid points sit on the VR conditioner analog front end where a silent open would disable crank-signal processing.","severity":"minor","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"work/erc/erc.json","locator":"by_type endpoint_off_grid=229; e.g. uuids 15d9afbe (286.385,107.315), 34654827 (R25 pin 1 at 107.315,80.01), c2f74bd3 (R34 pin 1 at 165.735,75.565)"},{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"all affected nets (Net-(R25-Pad1), Net-(U10-IN-) etc.) presently resolve with expected members"}],"reasoning":"No present-day connectivity fault is evidenced (DRC shows 0 unconnected items), so this is a latent-risk concern about schematic hygiene, not a defect in the saved netlist."},{"id":"PHY-007","title":"Hierarchy depends on disposable 'VR Conditioner.kicad_sch' byte-copy alias of the lowercase original","location":"project/VR Conditioner.kicad_sch (alias of VR conditioner.kicad_sch)","condition":"The candidate adds VR Conditioner.kicad_sch as a byte copy of the existing lowercase file so the 10-instance hierarchy resolves; ERC/netlist runs list project/VR Conditioner.kicad_sch and design.xml records sheet 4 source 'VR Conditioner.kicad_sch'. The declared limitations confirm the original checkout's filename discrepancy remains open.","mechanism":"Two byte-identical files with case-differing names coexist in the project. On case-insensitive filesystems they collide; on case-sensitive systems future edits can land in whichever copy a given tool resolves, silently forking the VR conditioner sheet (MAX9924 crank input chain, C23-C25, R25-R34, JP1). All connectivity verified here is against the alias, not the original file path.","severity":"minor","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"work/netlist/design.xml","locator":"sheet number 4 '/VR Conditioner/' source 'VR Conditioner.kicad_sch'"},{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"components C23-C25, R25-R34, U10, JP1 on sheet /VR Conditioner/ (uuid 76f66c7e-94ea-4f9a-aa2e-a01725934e38)"}],"reasoning":"The alias is explicitly declared as a disposable workaround, so this is not a new defect, but the physical design content of the VR conditioner now has two potential sources of truth; the verified netlist applies only to the alias as supplied."},{"id":"PHY-008","title":"Main CAN bus (CAN1) has no board-level ESD protection or filtering, unlike CAN2","location":"Root sheet nets /CAN+ and /CAN-","condition":"Nets /CAN+ (J1.47, J2.93) and /CAN- (J1.46, J2.94) run directly from the harness connector to the brain-module connector with no TVS, filter capacitors, or termination footprints on the base board, whereas CAN2 carries NUP2105L protectors (D10/D11), 47 pF filters, and terminator footprints.","mechanism":"If the Polygonus module does not include transceiver-side protection, the primary vehicle CAN lines enter the module unprotected against harness ESD/transients; the asymmetry versus CAN2 suggests protection was assumed to live on the module, which cannot be confirmed from this packet.","severity":"info","assessment":"concern","evidence":[{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"'/CAN+': [J1.47, J2.93]; '/CAN-': [J1.46, J2.94]; contrast '/CAN2+'/'/CAN2-' with D10/D11, C29/C30/C33/C34, R36/R37"}],"reasoning":"No requirement for base-board CAN1 protection is declared, and the module (out of scope) plausibly provides it, so this is recorded only as an informational observation about the asymmetric protection scheme and the coverage boundary, not as a fault."}]},"ttft_ms":114795,"type":"result","duration_ms":209545,"uuid":"0295336a-b473-48a3-b2cd-105595f2bc80","ttft_stream_ms":4715,"time_to_request_ms":306,"first_content_frame_ms":4715,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
